'''Vandor''', also known as '''Vandor-1''' or '''ID 53-80''', was a [[Temperature|cold]] frontier [[planet]] in the [[Sloo sector]] of [[the galaxy]]'s [[Mid Rim Territories|Mid Rim]]. Despite being sparsely settled, the [[Galactic Empire]] had a growing presence on the planet. [[Fort Ypso]] was a snowy [[mountain]] [[City|village]] located on Vandor.

==Description==
[[File:Vandor_databank.jpg|thumb|left|230px|The snowy landscape of Vandor]]
A [[Temperature|cold]] [[mountain]]ous [[planet]]<ref name="Databank" /> located in the [[Sloo sector]]<ref name="Tales" /> of the [[Mid Rim Territories|Mid Rim]],<ref name="Official Guide" /> in grid square P-14 on the [[Standard Galactic Grid]],<ref name="Coordinates" /> Vandor, sometimes known as Vandor-1<ref name="Topps">{{Topps|set=2018 Topps Countdown to Solo: A Star Wars Story|cardname=Beckett on the Snowy Plains of Vandor-1|link=https://www.tcdb.com/ViewCard.cfm/sid/175513/cid/11259542/2018-Topps-Countdown-to-Solo:-A-Star-Wars-Story-16-Beckett-on-the-Snowy-Plains-of-Vandor-1}}</ref> or ID 53-80,<ref name="Tales" /> The terrestrial planet [[orbit]]ed at least one [[star]],<ref name="Solo" /> with its [[Standard year|years]] lasting for 435 [[Standard day|days]].<ref name="Official Guide" /> It had two [[moon]]s,<ref name="Tales" /> a breathable [[atmosphere]],<ref name="Solo" /> and a diameter of 12,500 [[kilometer]]s. It lay relatively close to the secondary [[hyperspace route]] known as [[Gamor Run]].<ref name="Tales" />

The [[kod'yok]] were a [[Sentience|non-sentient]] [[species]] that roamed the plains of Vandor,<ref name="Official Guide" /> and [[luftgriff]]s were another creature found on the world.<ref name="Tales" />

==History==
===Early history===
The planet known as ID 53-80 was discovered by the [[Republic Scout Service]] and initially surveyed by the [[scout]] [[Arhul Corubalni]] centuries ago. Corubalni named the planet Vandor,<ref name="Tales" /> as a nod to an ancient poem about exploration<ref name="Official Guide" /> and filed the world log and surveys with the [[Republic Survey Corps]]. Arhul Corubalni recommended further surveys due to [[Lorahns Cavity]] and the [[Lesser Sloo Gas Cloud]] navigational hazards being the biggest negative factors preventing development and/or settlement.<ref name="Tales" /> At some point, the [[Frontier Skirmishes]] took place on Vandor.<ref name="Official Guide" />

An ambitious settlement attempt was made by the [[Ypsobay Trading Company]] that built [[Fort Ypso]] and various surrounding structures on the planet. However, the expansion attempt collapsed the organization<ref name="Official Guide" /> when the planet turned out to be too far from main trade routes to prosper. After a couple of generations most settlers left the world looking for a new home.<ref name="Tales" />

Before the [[Clone Wars]] while he was searching for new planets beyond<ref name="Tales" /> the [[Outer Rim Territories]]' [[Void of Chopani]]<ref name="RO Worlds">{{SW|url=news/where-in-the-galaxy-are-the-worlds-of-rogue-one|text=Where in the Galaxy Are the Worlds of ''Rogue One''?|int=Where in the Galaxy Are the Worlds of Rogue One?}}</ref> on the [[Vangaard Pathfinder]], [[Commerce Guild]] scout [[Tibbs Ospe]] discovered the Mid Rim planet tucked away in the ancient scout's report. With the changing realities of the [[hyperspace]] travel, Ospe figured Vandor could be a stopping place for [[Merchant|traders]] heading towards [[Deneba]] and [[Manda]].<ref name="Tales" /> Ospe fixed the ruins of [[Ypsobay Trading Company]]'s headquarters and started advertising that traders could find [[fuel]] and [[Foodstuff|food]] at Fort Ypso for their travels. At some point [[bartender]] [[Tivoche Bilure]] learned Ospe's story about Vandor and wrote it in his [[Midnight's book|journal]].<ref name="Tales" />

===Imperial Era===
Vandor was the site of an [[Imperial Garrison (Vandor)|Imperial Garrison]] during the [[Imperial Era|reign]] of the [[Galactic Empire]].<ref name="Star Wars 13">[[Star Wars (2020) 13|''Star Wars'' (2020) 13]]</ref> After Imperial [[stormtrooper]]s captured [[Landonis Balthazar Calrissian|Lando Calrissian's]] [[Starship|ship]], the ''[[Millennium Falcon]]'', they took it to be impounded on Vandor. A [[Standard week|week]] later, Calrissian and his [[droid]] [[L3-37]] arrived on Vandor, discovering the ''Falcon''{{'s}} location. Planning to rescue his ship, Calrissian decided to bide his time by playing a game of [[sabacc]] in [[the Lodge]], using [[Galactic Credit Standard|credits]] he had received from completing a [[Job on Kullgroon|recent mission]].<ref name="Lando 5">[[Lando - Double or Nothing 5|''Lando - Double or Nothing'' 5]]</ref>

At the same time, [[Tobias Beckett]] and [[Beckett's gang|his crew]] had also landed on Vandor to carry out a [[Heist on Vandor|heist]] on an [[Galactic Empire|Imperial]] [[20-T Railcrawler conveyex transport|conveyex]] [[train]], in order to acquire [[coaxium]] for [[Dryden Vos]] and [[Crimson Dawn]]. They were assisted by [[Han Solo]] and [[Chewbacca]], who had escaped [[Mimban]] on Beckett's stolen [[Y-45 armored transport hauler]]. The heist ultimately failed due to the interference of [[Enfys Nest]]'s [[Cloud-Riders]], who also attempted to steal the coaxium, leading Solo to drop the cargo in order to save the survivors of Beckett's crew.<ref name="Solo" />

After Vos' [[yacht]] ''[[First Light]]'' traveled to Vandor to personally meet Beckett, the crew planned a [[Raid on Kessel|second mission]] to [[Kessel]] so they could retrieve coaxium to replace the cargo lost during the heist. Needing a ship that was fast enough to make the [[Kessel Run]], the crew visited the Lodge, where they met Calrissian. At the Lodge, Solo joined a game of sabacc against Calrissian, hoping to win the ''Millennium Falcon''. However, Calrissian's cheating led Solo to lose against him, but he eventually agreed to take Beckett's crew to Kessel aboard his ship.<ref name="Solo" />

==Inhabitants==
Vandor was sparsely settled, lacking the technological infrastructure that was present on other worlds. The Galactic Empire had begun to have a presence on Vandor, however,<ref name="Databank" /> transporting cargo across the planet's mountains with conveyex trains.<ref name="Solo" />

==Locations==
The terrain of Vandor was made up of various mountains,<ref name="Solo" /> including [[Mount Vastadon]], [[Mount Redolava]], and the [[Iridium Mountains]], which contained the [[Crispin Imperial Depository]].<ref name="Official Guide" /> The planet was also home to the village of [[Fort Ypso]], which contained the Lodge, a saloon with a [[gambling]] hall and a droid-fighting arena.<ref name="Ultimate Guide" /> Other locations on Vandor included [[Corubalni Spaceport]],<ref name="Tales" /> [[Corubalni Pass]], and the [[Spinnaker Trail]].<ref name="Official Guide" />

==Behind the scenes==
Vandor was created for the [[2018]] [[Star Wars Anthology Series|''Star Wars'' film]] ''[[Solo: A Star Wars Story]]''. The first footage of the planet was shown in the "Big Game" Super Bowl TV spot released on [[February 4]], [[2018]].<ref name="Solo TV Spot">{{SWYouTube|9Szts88zY4o|Solo: A Star Wars Story "Big Game" TV Spot (:45)|sw_url=video/big-game-tv-spot-solo-a-star-wars-story}}</ref> It was later also identified as [[Vandor-1]],<ref name="Topps" /> a planet that was first mentioned in ''[[Coruscant and the Core Worlds]]'', a [[2003]] sourcebook for the now-[[Star Wars Legends|Legends]] ''[[Star Wars Roleplaying Game]]''.<ref name="Core">''[[Coruscant and the Core Worlds]]''</ref> In ''[[Solo: A Star Wars Story The Official Guide]]'', Vandor is placed in the [[Mid Rim Territories|Mid Rim]], rather than in the [[Core Worlds]].<ref name="Official Guide" />

Early inspirations for the look of Vandor in ''Solo'' came from art of the American West by late-19th-century painter [[Wikipedia:Frederic Remington|Frederic Remington]], particularly the [[1900s|1906]] painting ''A Taint on the Wind'', and the 20th-century illustrator [[Wikipedia:Robert McGinnis|Robert McGinnis]]. Another inspiration for Vandor were the lavish landscapes of the American West by the 19th-century painters [[Wikipedia:Frederick Church|Frederick Church]] and [[Wikipedia:Albert Bierstadt|Albert Bierstadt]].<ref name="Art of Solo">''[[The Art of Solo: A Star Wars Story]]''</ref> The environment of Vandor was designed to evoke the landscape of southern [[Wikipedia:Colorado|Colorado's]] rocky mountains, as intended by screenwriter [[Jon Kasdan]], who believed that it fit with the space-western feeling he and the film's crew tried to evoke.<ref name="Jon's Twitter">{{Twitter|JonKasdan|status/1040529501870944256|[[Jon Kasdan]]|quote=In honor of the digital release of #SoloAStarWarsStory & in lieu of a commentary, here are 53 random factoids & notes about the making & writing for anybody who's interested. If you haven't seen the movie yet... maybe watch it before reading? Anyway, enjoy the movie & #MTFBWY|archivefile=File:Jon-Kasdan-SoloFacts-September-14-2018.png}}</ref>

